infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two ways to break the dependency array
  desc Both misdeclare what the effect reads — React compares deps element by element with Object.is
  compares
    - label Unstable reference in deps
      children
        - label Inline object / array / function
          desc Fresh identity created every render
        - label Object.is(prev, next) is false
          desc Reference compare fails on every render
        - label 30 renders trigger 30 re-runs
          desc Chart or socket rebuilt 30 times while scrolling
        - label Wasted teardown + setup churn
          desc Effect destroyed and recreated each commit
        - label Fix: primitives, build inside, memoize
          desc Depend on the values inside, or useMemo the object
    - label Value omitted from deps
      children
        - label Reads a value not in deps
          desc The I-only-want-this-on-mount excuse
        - label Object.is never sees it change
          desc Effect keeps the first render's value forever
        - label Frozen stale closure
          desc Old query fetched on every keystroke
        - label Silent wrong data, no crash
          desc No error log — ships straight to production
        - label Fix: move out, ref, restructure
          desc exhaustive-deps is a correctness check, not style
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
